      "type": "physical_space",
      "description": "A wooden discrimination box (94 cm long, 30 cm wide, 11.5 cm deep) divided into a nest-box, an entrance chamber, and two electric boxes (one white, one black). The white and black cards were interchangeable. Electric shock was delivered via wires on the floor of the electric boxes.",
      "n_stimuli": null,
      "source": "p. 1-2, Figure 1, Figure 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "other",
      "description": "Electric shock stimulus of varying strengths, generated by a Porter inductorium. Calibrated in 'units of stimulation' (Martin's unit). Strengths used: 125±10, 300±25, 500±50, 135, 195, 255, 375, 420 units.",
