      "source": "p. 8-9, Table 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "visual_form",
      "description": "Visual discrimination conditions (white vs. black electric boxes) varied in difficulty by altering brightness difference: Set I (medium difficulty), Set II (easy/great difference), Set III (difficult/slight difference). This was achieved by modifying internal cardboard configurations and open space for light entry.",
